From 2cc4aefc40fdacdabf23c9d232704e6ab406bb7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 19:44:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix root cause: frontend built from a stale committed bundle,
 not src/
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Found the real reason every frontend rebuild served identical output
no matter what changed in src/, across six version bumps and a full
repository remove/re-add: frontend/index.html and a frontend/assets/
folder containing an already-built JS/CSS bundle had been committed
as if they were source, back when the local add-on's files were first
migrated into this git repo (present from that very first commit).
Vite's build entry (rollupOptions.input: index.html) followed that
file's <script src="./assets/main-*.js"> tag straight to the frozen
pre-built bundle instead of the real entry point at src/main.tsx —
so `npm run build` was deterministically re-processing the same old
frozen code every time (confirmed: "5 modules transformed" instead of
the real ~2750), completely blind to every src/ edit made since,
including all of Fas 4b.

Fix: restore index.html to the standard Vite entry
(<script type="module" src="/src/main.tsx">) and delete the stale
frontend/assets/ folder — it doesn't belong in source control at all
(it's build output). Verified locally: a clean build now transforms
~2750 modules and the output actually contains "Nibe F750",
"Lyxläge varmvatten", "watchdog_reset", and the build-diagnostic
marker from the previous two rollout attempts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01D9yfcLt9RHbqoZD18y9PT7
